    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2024-june/q3",
      "question": "<p><strong>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</strong></p><p><strong>Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</strong></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:75mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-01-2024-june/q03-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. A circle C containing a three-lobed pool P, unshaded, centred at the centre of the circle; the region T between the pool edge and the circle is shaded.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows the design for a bathing pool.</p><p>The pool, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, shown unshaded in Figure 1, is surrounded by a tiled area, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 1.</p><p>The tiled area is bounded by the edge of the pool and by a circle, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, with radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>.</p><p>The centre of the pool and the centre of the circle are the same point.</p><p>The edge of the pool is modelled by the curve with polar equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=4-a\\sin3\\theta\\qquad0\\leqslant\\theta\\leqslant2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a positive constant.</p><p>Given that the shortest distance between the edge of the pool and the circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.5\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Hence, using algebraic integration, determine, according to the model, the exact area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
