      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2024-june/q4",
      "question": "<p>The complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=\\mathrm e^{\\mathrm i\\theta}\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> is real.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^n+\\frac{1}{z^n}\\equiv2\\cos n\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> is a positive integer.</p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos^5\\theta=\\frac{1}{16}(\\cos5\\theta+5\\cos3\\theta+10\\cos\\theta)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Hence, making your reasoning clear, determine all the solutions of<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos5\\theta+5\\cos3\\theta+12\\cos\\theta=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
