      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2024-june/q7",
      "question": "<p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\mathbf i-2\\mathbf j+3\\mathbf k+\\lambda(2\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j-4\\mathbf k)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=5\\mathbf i+p\\mathbf j-7\\mathbf k+\\mu(6\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j+8\\mathbf k)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\"></span> are scalar parameters and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span> contains <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that the vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\mathbf i-10\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k\"></span> is perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Hence determine a Cartesian equation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Hence determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> intersect at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span></li><li>the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(12,-11,6)\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>determine, to the nearest degree, the acute angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
