      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2024-june/q8",
      "question": "<p>A scientist is studying the effect of introducing a population of type <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> bacteria into a population of type <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> bacteria.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> days, the number of type <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> bacteria, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>, and the number of type <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> bacteria, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>, are modelled by the differential equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}=x+y\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt}=3y-2x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm d^2x}{\\mathrm dt^2}-4\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}+5x=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Determine a general solution for the number of type <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> bacteria at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> days. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Determine a general solution for the number of type <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> bacteria at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> days. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The model predicts that, at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> hours, the number of bacteria in the two populations will be equal.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=100\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=275\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>, giving your answer to 2 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Suggest a limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
